    52	
    53	- Chunks 1–4 and 6–33: runner, one manifest cell.
    54	- Chunk 5: the same no-flash launcher directly invokes the exact probe target/argv under the same guard, identity and reservation gates.
    55	- After the probe process closes its raw log, a non-logged finalization step hashes that final log, writes the campaign/backend/overlay/launcher/log provenance into the JSON, regenerates `.sha256`, and runs `PROBE_CONTRACT_BF`.
    56	- Only successful finalization and validation mark chunk 5 gate-complete.
    57	
    58	### HIGH 4 — child-process import isolation is not fully contracted
    59	
    60	The launcher is fail-closed for the parent. Fork and normal multiprocessing spawn preserve the explicit path, but a fresh `subprocess` Python interpreter reconstructs its path from argv/environment and would not inherit the launcher’s in-memory `sys.path`.
    61	
    62	The implementation contract should require one of:
    63	
    64	- no independently exec’d Python children in the pinned evaluator/probe tree;
    65	- every such child runs through the launcher; or
    66	- a controlled child environment plus a child-side origin/backend assertion.
